-- title:
--   Order zero at cuspidal places for nonvanishing cusp limits
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \ge 1$ and let $\mathbb{C}F_N =$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange ℂ (ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFull N)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) be the subfield of $\mathbb{C}((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $\mathbb{C}$ the coefficientwise images under `coeffEmb ℂ` (the map $\mathbb{Q}((q)) \to \mathbb{C}((q))$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to \mathbb{C}$) of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the series `qExpand ℚ d jq` for the nonzero divisors $d \mid N$. Let $x \in \mathbb{C}F_N$ and let $F : \mathfrak{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ be a function such that for every $\tau \in \mathfrak{H}$ the functions $z \mapsto F(\mathrm{ofComplex}\, z)$ and $z \mapsto$ `realize N x (ofComplex z)` agree on a punctured neighbourhood of $\tau$ in $\mathbb{C}$; here `realize N x` sends $\tau$ to $g(\tau)/h(\tau)$ for some pair $g, h$ of modular forms of a common weight $k$ on $\Gamma_0(N)$ with $h(\tau) \neq 0$ and $x \cdot \tilde h = \tilde g$ in $\mathbb{C}((q))$ ($\tilde{\,\cdot\,}$ denoting the $q$-expansion at width $1$), and to $0$ if no such pair exists. Assume that for every $\sigma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ there is $L \neq 0$ with $F(\sigma \cdot \tau) \to L$ as $\operatorname{im} \tau \to \infty$. Let $v$ be a place of $\mathbb{C}F_N$ over $\mathbb{C}$, that is, a valuation subring of $\mathbb{C}F_N$ which contains the image of $\mathbb{C}$, is not all of $\mathbb{C}F_N$, and is a principal ideal ring, and assume that the element `coeffEmb ℂ jq` (the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$, which lies in $\mathbb{C}F_N$) does not belong to that valuation subring. Then $v.\mathrm{ord}\, x = 0$, the order being $-\log$ of the value of $x$ under the adic valuation attached to $v$.
--
--   Classically this says that a meromorphic function on $X_0(N)$ whose associated function on the upper half plane has a finite nonzero limit at every cusp $\sigma(i\infty)$, $\sigma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, has neither zero nor pole at any cuspidal place, the cuspidal places being those at which $j$ has a pole. It is used in the dictionary between places of $\mathbb{C}(X_0(N))$ and points of the Riemann surface, in particular by [`ModularCurve.ComplexPlaceDictionary.isPrincipal_of_abelJacobi_mem_periodLattice`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ComplexPlaceDictionary.isPrincipal_of_abelJacobi_mem_periodLattice).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_ord_eq_zero_of_jq_not_mem_of_realize_tendsto.lean

